{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531441-dread-names-red-list","id":1531441,"title":"Dread Names, Red List","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-24T15:56:28-08:00","id":1531441,"title":"Dread Names, Red List","content":"Hey folks,<br /> <br /> I've been on a bit of a roll, re-reading all of the V20 books in my collection. It will, I'm fairly sure, be considered the height of the V:TM line from future generations because it nicely combines fidelity to the lore as well as a coherent vision for what is to come.<br /> <br /> So, I felt another thread needed to be discussed and that's THE RED LIST. I've never had a chance to use any of the Red Listers in my game but I've always liked reading about them and the massive amount of world building they add.<br /> <br /> Basically, the Red List is where a lot of the 2nd Edition gonzo-ness has gone and I think it makes it extra special. It existed prior to this book but I think this is where it was really all came together into an element of the setting that I have in the backrgound even if I don't think it's a central one in my campaign (yet).<br /> <br /> Favorite stuff:<br /> <br /> * Ayisha Jocastian is my favorite character as I love someone explaining why so many copies of the Book of Nod will have proliferated throughout the setting.<br /> <br /> * Karen Anatos as a kind of Ingrid Pitt and immortal vampire actress operating in plain sight.<br /> <br /> * Arctos from the Hunter's Hunted getting an update and being treated as a terrifying figure threatening the vampire stability (I wonder if he would be a full on Awakened in a crossover game)<br /> <br /> * Germaine, who I think is meant to be the one from the Clan Book Tremere.<br /> <br /> * The Typhoid Mary element of Rabbat.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T04:57:20-08:00","id":1531505,"title":"","content":"Some questions about the Red List<br /> <br /> Gratiano - why did he never become anathema? his coup raised the Anarchist Revolt<br /> <br /> Velya and Vykos - why did they never become Anathema? They are original leaders of the anarch Tzimisce, they created Valderie, the greatest anarch instrument during the war, I won't include Lugoj for obvious reasons (the man was abducted by the Elder himself)<br /> <br /> Ur Shulgi - Hakim's son broke the Tremere curse and caused the Assamite schism, the Tremere clan and Tegyrius as Justicar would have more than enough reasons to mark him on the Red List (he is powerful, yes he is, just like Kemintiri and Enkidu )<br /> <br /> Goratrix - why was Goratrix never named Anathema? the man led the rebellious Tremere into the Sabbat, practically giving the clan's greatest tool to the enemy sect<br /> <br /> Ankla Hotep - someone who alters reality and pretends to be Cain should at least attract the attention of the Inner Circle, in one of the sect's Ventrue bastions of power, Berlin<br /> <br /> Tyler - Patricia Bollinbroke was there at Thorns, and attempted on Hardestad's unlife, twice, succeeding at least once, she may have had an alternative identity or acquired amnesty, but I still always saw her as a potential anathema<br /> <br /> Xaviar - the Justicar accused the Inner Circle of ignoring the threat of the antidiluvians and openly confronted the elders and caused the clan's exile from the sect, Karsh himself accused him of being a traitor, he could be a potential anathema.<br /> <br /> Marcus Vitel - the old man pretended to be Ventrue for a long time, operated in the Camarilla as Prince of DC, later turned the city into an independent stronghold, and the Inner Circle did nothing? another potential anathema<br /> <br /> Montgomery Coven - committed diablerie on Mithras, okay, many Camarilla elders didn't like the anachronism of Mithras and his position as an iron fist in the islands, but look, his presence was a sign of Camarilla power in London for generations, besides, Coven and a potential new Regent of the Sabbat in Europe as Mithras dominates Monty's will and mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T06:48:17-08:00","id":1531509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531441-dread-names-red-list?p=1531505#post1531505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some questions about the Red List<br /> <br /> Gratiano - why did he never become anathema? his coup raised the Anarchist Revolt<br /> <br /> Velya and Vykos - why did they never become Anathema? They are original leaders of the anarch Tzimisce, they created Valderie, the greatest anarch instrument during the war, I won't include Lugoj for obvious reasons (the man was abducted by the Elder himself)<br /> <br /> Ur Shulgi - Hakim's son broke the Tremere curse and caused the Assamite schism, the Tremere clan and Tegyrius as Justicar would have more than enough reasons to mark him on the Red List (he is powerful, yes he is, just like Kemintiri and Enkidu )<br /> <br /> Goratrix - why was Goratrix never named Anathema? the man led the rebellious Tremere into the Sabbat, practically giving the clan's greatest tool to the enemy sect<br /> <br /> Ankla Hotep - someone who alters reality and pretends to be Cain should at least attract the attention of the Inner Circle, in one of the sect's Ventrue bastions of power, Berlin<br /> <br /> Tyler - Patricia Bollinbroke was there at Thorns, and attempted on Hardestad's unlife, twice, succeeding at least once, she may have had an alternative identity or acquired amnesty, but I still always saw her as a potential anathema<br /> <br /> Xaviar - the Justicar accused the Inner Circle of ignoring the threat of the antidiluvians and openly confronted the elders and caused the clan's exile from the sect, Karsh himself accused him of being a traitor, he could be a potential anathema.<br /> <br /> Marcus Vitel - the old man pretended to be Ventrue for a long time, operated in the Camarilla as Prince of DC, later turned the city into an independent stronghold, and the Inner Circle did nothing? another potential anathema<br /> <br /> Montgomery Coven - committed diablerie on Mithras, okay, many Camarilla elders didn't like the anachronism of Mithras and his position as an iron fist in the islands, but look, his presence was a sign of Camarilla power in London for generations, besides, Coven and a potential new Regent of the Sabbat in Europe as Mithras dominates Monty's will and mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like in-universe, a lot of the Red List is driven directly by the politics of the Camarilla and the fact that Kindred society is incredibly hypocritical. The Red List as a public thing didn't exist until the 19th century and previously was just a hit list that the Inner Council assembled to deal with and only the Justicars knew about. It was a nickname for the people the Camarilla wanted dead and not an actual policy-policy.<br /> <br /> By the time it came out as an actual thing-thing when Ventrue Justicar Michaelis was murdered and replaced by Kemintiri, humiliating the entirety of the Camarilla. The list has since been compromised of five kinds of Kindred.<br /> <br /> * Old as shit methusalehs who refuse to get with the program of the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> * Masquerade violators who are just plain annoyances like that one Gangrel horror actress and Aiysha Jocastian.<br /> <br /> * Infernalists and other people who challenge the whole secular worldview of the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> * People who have pissed off someone in the Clan completely that they have decided to turn the entire Camarilla against them.<br /> <br /> * Vampire Hunters of a level that can't be stopped ala Ciaphas Cain or Ossian.<br /> <br /> My take on the subject is the Camarilla will generally exclude the following:<br /> <br /> * Members of the Sabbat's leadership: All of the Sabbat have Blood Hunts on them by nature since they're an enemy sect so it's really kind of pointless. &quot;We want this guy EVEN MORE DEAD than our present kill-on-sight&quot; order.<br /> <br /> * People who are politically connected: Gustav Brendenstein is a vampire who supported Hitler and staked a bunch of Archons and other ridiculous bullshit that seems to still be canon or has been recanonized. Yet, he's still an Old Boy Ventrue so the Camarilla will give him a pass.<br /> <br /> * People whose crimes are secret: Tyler didn't kill Hardestadt (because he's right there!) and later accepted the pardon of the Anarchs since she didn't join the Sabbat at Thorns. Monty Coven is not known as the guy who killed Mithras. Marcus Vitel isn't on the Red List because until Beckett's Jyhad Diary, everyone assumed he was ALREADY dead instead of being in torpor for twenty years.<br /> <br /> * People who you might want to win over: If Gratiano defected to the Camarilla, he'd be welcomed with open arms. So are a bunch of elders on the other side of the Anarchs and Sabbat. You could put out a kill order on the Old Man of the Mountain or other Assamites but maybe you'd like the Assamites to join some day. It's why killing Xavier would only piss the Gangrel off more and make reconciliation impossible.<br /> <br /> * People you can't kill because it's fucking impossible: Kemintiri and Petaniqua are on the Red List from the beginning and still on it a century later because they're fucking invincible. It's like putting Baba Yaga on the list or Ur-Shulgi. Yeah, you COULD but what';s the point as no one can fucking get rid of either so it just embarrasses the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T08:50:11-08:00","id":1531522,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not going to lie, Arctos is far too delightful as \u2018Slightly Evil DOCTOR STRANGE\u2019 for me to imagine him as anything but one of the Awakened - it\u2019s also amusing to wonder how the allies mentioned in his HUNTERS HUNTED appearance fit into the MAGE: THE AWAKENING paradigms.<br /> <br /> He\u2019s even more fun if you assume his mind-controlled vampires are more like post-chip Spike/William the Bloody than mindless robots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T23:53:05-08:00","id":1531600,"title":"","content":"Seems in general that most Vampires on the Red List are ones that are outside the usual sect and clan structure. Meaning that there is not much of a political backlash if you kill them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T11:57:12-08:00","id":1531639,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12210\" data-vbnamecard=\"12210\">Ulisses</a> I always go with with the mindset is what the Camarilla wants and what they can actually do are two very different things. The sect doesn't have large standing armies at there beck and call to go after Red Listers as many of them are very old and powerful and reside deep in enemy terrority which also plays apart why many of the most wanted are still around.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T13:54:34-08:00","id":1531646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531441-dread-names-red-list?p=1531639#post1531639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12210\" data-vbnamecard=\"12210\">Ulisses</a> I always go with with the mindset is what the Camarilla wants and what they can actually do are two very different things. The sect doesn't have large standing armies at there beck and call to go after Red Listers as many of them are very old and powerful and reside deep in enemy terrority which also plays apart why many of the most wanted are still around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take the Red List as something of a vanity project over all that exists to, yes, get rid of enemies of the Camarilla but also pat themselves on the back for eliminating.<br /> <br /> Get all of those Archons something to obsess over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T23:36:13-08:00","id":1531666,"title":"","content":"The Camarilla doesn't put Ur-Shulgi or Xavier on the Red List, because the Camarilla doesn't want to effectively declare war on either Clan. They have enough problems, without creating even more enemies.<br /> <br /> Obviously, Ur-Shulgi isn't exactly a friend of the Camarilla. But at least at the moment, the Web of Knives, under his direction, represent a problem mostly for the Banu Haqim within the Camarilla, or for those Kindred unlucky enough to be eaten by rogue Assamites reveling in the removal of the Tremere Curse. The Camarilla as a whole doesn't really care, and don't want to be dragged into what, to them, seems like an internal Clan Assamite matter.<br /> <br /> Xavier, meanwhile, had enough pull among Gangrel to effect a mass exodus. The Camarilla would rather those Gangrel <i>come back</i>. Not be incited into making war on the Camarilla instead. Gangrel know too much about Camarilla defenses to be safe to alienate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 02-28-2024, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T04:09:18-08:00","id":1531673,"title":"","content":"Kindred society being what it is, there's also the fact to remember that the Red List is a big PUBLIC statement of wanting someone dead and hardly is necessary for actually WANTING someone dead.<br /> <br /> Xavier undoubtedly has to deal with a bunch of assassins from various parties without anyone actually claiming credit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T12:32:01-08:00","id":1531690,"title":"","content":"Or said beings have made plenty of enemies with other supernaturals and mortals and sooner or later one of them will get lucky. So why risk your own precious neck if you have other options on the table. That said it's just public relations statement is that this kindred is really bad even by our standards and should be avoided as much as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T21:24:36-08:00","id":1531723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531441-dread-names-red-list?p=1531505#post1531505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why did he never become anathema?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the real answer is meta-narrative. While I have not read Dread Names, Red List, I have read the Kindred's Most Wanted which is its precursor. And while it had a prestige format, it was still clearly a game sourcebook, not a piece of game fiction. The quarry in KMW were characters clearly meant to give STs something to run in their home chronicles.<br /> <br /> What would the PCs do if they found out that Rabbat, Enkidu, Ossian, Ferox, Petaniqua, etc. had entered their domain. What would be the signs that indicated their arrival? How long would it be before NPCs or the PCs noticed it? Would they investigate and find out the cause? What would they do upon contact?<br /> <br /> All the vampires of KMW could be imagined as wandering solitary outlaws that might arrive in any chronicle's domain. Major Sabbat NPCs like Gratiano or Goratrix would clearly not. Those NPCs would dwell in safety in their lairs and never come out.<br /> <br /> Once you interpret these books as a resource for the ST, it all makes sense.<br /> <br /> The Kindred of KMW and DNRL are not meant to be authoritative. Obviously other vampires are included. Perhaps even the vampires you mentioned. But as a resource for the gamemaster, there's only those NPCs who could be easily introduced into any chronicle because that is the purpose of the sourcebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T14:14:30-08:00","id":1531742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531441-dread-names-red-list?p=1531723#post1531723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the real answer is meta-narrative. While I have not read Dread Names, Red List, I have read the Kindred's Most Wanted which is its precursor. And while it had a prestige format, it was still clearly a game sourcebook, not a piece of game fiction. The quarry in KMW were characters clearly meant to give STs something to run in their home chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the meta narrative is tied to the role that was created for the story.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, the Red List is defined by its role as an RPG bunch of antagonists so its inseparable from its story role.<br /> <br /> Hydra exists OOC so a bunch of superheroes can punch and kill Nazis that otherwise don't kill anyone even in modern day. That doesn't mean that it's meaningless to examine why even Spider-Man is okay blowing up a Hydra base.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T15:18:30-08:00","id":1531747,"title":"","content":"RPGs aren't stories. They are games. The only &quot;story&quot; that emerges from an RPG is the one collectively created at the gaming table by the various contributions of its players and gamemaster. The &quot;story&quot; is created <i>post hoc</i> by the decisions made during the game and the players and GM looking back at how the game developed to its conclusion, <u>not</u> <i>ex ante</i> by the intentions of the gamemaster or gaming company ignoring the decisions by the players whenever they go against what was planned. (The GM may have intentions or predictions of the most likely responses of the PCs to help them prepare the game, but should never ignore them in favor of what the ST intended.)<br /> <br /> Whenever a gamemaster decides he is going to create a &quot;story&quot; - meaning she will invalidate the actions taken by the players if they go against what she intended to happen - inevitably the player's enjoyment of the game suffers because their choices become meaningless. It becomes a form of passive entertainment instead of active entertainment where they make decisions. Whenever a gaming company decides to hijack their RPG setting by forcing through setting changes by metaplot because of their &quot;story&quot;, it inevitably divides the gaming community and their fan base because it ends up invalidating how their individual campaigns decided things.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I have not read DNRL, so I cannot evaluate it. But KMW was clearly written with the intent of STs being able to take the characters described there and use them at their own gaming tables. It was not intended to be an anthology of stories that couldn't be reasonably used by any ST. So it didn't include figures that could reasonably be expected to be on the Red List, but couldn't be used at the game table because it simply would not make sense for those NPCs to appear in any chronicle.<br /> <br /> This is different from the similar prestige format of Children of the Inquisition which is obviously a lorebook designed to introduce more backstory to the setting. But even here, because the focus is on the past/background of these NPCs and not what they are doing at this moment which is going to change the game setting, it is still intended for use by the GM in whatever way she wants. Certainly you just couldn't place every single NPC in CotI into just any chronicle. But it would allow an ST who wanted to include the PCs meeting one of these important NPCs to be able to portray that NPC because the ST now has better understanding of their background and personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T15:35:48-08:00","id":1531751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531441-dread-names-red-list?p=1531747#post1531747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RPGs aren't stories. They are games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to undercut your point but, uh, it's called the Storyteller System for a reason. The &quot;game&quot; is an interactive story created between the Storyteller and the players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T14:26:42-08:00","id":1531978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531441-dread-names-red-list?p=1531505#post1531505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some questions about the Red List<br /> <br /> Gratiano - why did he never become anathema? his coup raised the Anarchist Revolt<br /> <br /> Outside of possibly diablizing his sire and even that is questionable, I don't think he has done much since then to warrant a place on the Red List and the Revolt was already going to happen regardless of his actions.<br /> <br /> Velya and Vykos - why did they never become Anathema? They are original leaders of the anarch Tzimisce, they created Valderie, the greatest anarch instrument during the war, I won't include Lugoj for obvious reasons (the man was abducted by the Elder himself)<br /> <br /> Simple they are both old and to potent and deep into there homelands to be taken out.<br /> <br /> Ur Shulgi - Hakim's son broke the Tremere curse and caused the Assamite schism, the Tremere clan and Tegyrius as Justicar would have more than enough reasons to mark him on the Red List (he is powerful, yes he is, just like Kemintiri and Enkidu )<br /> <br /> Same reason as above and nobody sane wants to take on one of the oldest and most potent blood mages in the world of darkness and the leadership of the sect would see this as internal clan politics and not want to get into the middle of it.<br /> <br /> Goratrix - why was Goratrix never named Anathema? the man led the rebellious Tremere into the Sabbat, practically giving the clan's greatest tool to the enemy sect<br /> <br /> I'd go with the fact that the Sabbat already had potent blood magics with the Fiends and others that it would be a moot point to say that it changed things that much.<br /> <br /> Ankla Hotep - someone who alters reality and pretends to be Cain should at least attract the attention of the Inner Circle, in one of the sect's Ventrue bastions of power, Berlin<br /> <br /> I can't answer that.<br /> <br /> Tyler - Patricia Bollinbroke was there at Thorns, and attempted on Hardestad's unlife, twice, succeeding at least once, she may have had an alternative identity or acquired amnesty, but I still always saw her as a potential anathema.<br /> <br /> She joined the Camarilla later and did her part in making the sect stronger in the city and most outside the inner circle don't know about Hardstadt the Younger and Elder being different Kindred. They probably thought she might have taken steps to protect herself if she suddenly was taken out.<br /> <br /> Xaviar - the Justicar accused the Inner Circle of ignoring the threat of the antidiluvians and openly confronted the elders and caused the clan's exile from the sect, Karsh himself accused him of being a traitor, he could be a potential anathema.<br /> <br /> Considering that he suffered final death and acknowleding he was right about the threat would serve no purpose to put him on the list.<br /> <br /> Marcus Vitel - the old man pretended to be Ventrue for a long time, operated in the Camarilla as Prince of DC, later turned the city into an independent stronghold, and the Inner Circle did nothing? another potential anathema<br /> <br /> To old and powerful and at this point they wouldn't be able to do much.<br /> <br /> Montgomery Coven - committed diablerie on Mithras, okay, many Camarilla elders didn't like the anachronism of Mithras and his position as an iron fist in the islands, but look, his presence was a sign of Camarilla power in London for generations, besides, Coven and a potential new Regent of the Sabbat in Europe as Mithras dominates Monty's will and mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most don't know that Mithras was consumed by Coven and even then he held little interest in sects and when he started to gain stronger control of the Banu Haqim neonate, he was already thinking of ways to retake the city for himself and the sects be damned. In fact I'd bet many thought that Coven was just a catspaw of the Ventrue and not the ancient himself. Many kindred hadn't seen him for along time and wouldn't know about the new body.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T20:26:52-08:00","id":1531992,"title":"","content":"Killing Xavier would be monumentally stupid. By default, Gangrel are largely irrelevant. They wander the interstates and forests, feeding on truck-drivers and hikers. Motivating them to come into the cities seeking revenge would be staggeringly stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T06:52:56-08:00","id":1532019,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d argue that Gangrel tend to be apolitical, but they can be pretty darned relevant if they decide to start hunting YOUR coterie!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T06:54:52-08:00","id":1532022,"title":"","content":"On a more serious note, dear readers, if you were asked to add a name to the Red List, which name would you provide and how much do you think it would cost to put it there? (In terms Camarilla deal-making).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T08:57:00-08:00","id":1532039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531441-dread-names-red-list?p=1532022#post1532022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more serious note, dear readers, if you were asked to add a name to the Red List, which name would you provide and how much do you think it would cost to put it there? (In terms Camarilla deal-making).</div> </div> </div> </div>Theo Bell should be a candidate for the Red List but I also believe someone should be protecting him. Probably whoever got him to assassinate Hardestadt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T12:20:15-08:00","id":1532050,"title":"","content":"Outside of Theo Bell for betraying the Camarilla and sending Hardstadt The Younger &amp; Jan to their final deaths, I can't really think of anyone who is awful or dangerous enough for such a posting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T13:49:12-08:00","id":1532056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531441-dread-names-red-list?p=1532050#post1532050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of Theo Bell for betraying the Camarilla and sending Hardstadt The Younger &amp; Jan to their final deaths, I can't really think of anyone who is awful or dangerous enough for such a posting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some possibilities:<br /> <br /> Felicity Price since humans CAN be on the list. She's the head of the American Second inquisition.<br /> <br /> Monty Coven if he's proven to have been behind the Cleansing of London as a way to get his revenge on Anne Bowesley.<br /> <br /> Baba Yaga if it's true that she survived according to Beckett's Jyhad Diary.<br /> <br /> Beckett because Hardestadt <i>really</i> wanted him dead.<br /> <br /> Marcus Vitel for taking Washington DC for the Anarchs.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T15:06:05-08:00","id":1532063,"title":"","content":"All good ideas for the Red List, but I think that it's quite likely that Coven has eliminated any possible leaks about his role in the purge of London. As for Beckett it could happen but I think it's not likely as with Hardstadt gone and most Kindred are not going to care about the ventrue elder posing as his sire in the early nights of the sect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T18:54:08-08:00","id":1532069,"title":"","content":"I think Camarilla would really look for the bastards who blew their meeting with the Setites (that blundered the Clan's entry in the sect). But... who knows.<br /> <br /> Somehow, I think Carna would be hunted. Even now I don't really understand if House Carna is Anarch or what, but for me it makes sense for her to be Anarch and be considered suspect number one for Vienna Zero, besides being someone capable of breaking Blood Bonds (Sabbat business).<br /> <br /> I like Xaviar being hunted, and yes that would be stupid, but on-point too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T19:49:44-08:00","id":1532071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531441-dread-names-red-list?p=1532069#post1532069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Camarilla would really look for the bastards who blew their meeting with the Setites (that blundered the Clan's entry in the sect). But... who knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an ST, I suspect they wouldn't look very hard because the people who did it are almost certainly the Banu Haqim's leadership.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can have us or the Setites.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Somehow, I think Carna would be hunted. Even now I don't really understand if House Carna is Anarch or what, but for me it makes sense for her to be Anarch and be considered suspect number one for Vienna Zero, besides being someone capable of breaking Blood Bonds (Sabbat business).<br /> <br /> I like Xaviar being hunted, and yes that would be stupid, but on-point too. </div> </div> </div>My assumption is that House Carna isn't necessarily Anarch after the Vienna chantry lost its ability to tell the local Prince not to take any aid from its members. Carna being a former Prince herself certainly has the same disdain for Anarchs as most Elders.<br /> <br /> But plenty of Neonates will join the Anarchs among House Carna anyway because it is the best deal if you're not an Elder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T07:09:36-08:00","id":1532078,"title":"","content":"Undeath of the Author: My intention with the Setite/Ministry hotel explosion was that all fingers would point to the Banu Haqim as you say, but in actual fact the perpetrators were reporting to the Toreador Justicar. A lot of Camarilla Toreador already have peddling vice and manipulating lusts wrapped up in their portfolio, and they saw no reason to risk their powerbase by introducing the Ministry to their ranks. Publicly though, they were as shocked as the other Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T07:27:35-08:00","id":1532079,"title":"","content":"Thanks for that info!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T09:05:21-08:00","id":1532086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531441-dread-names-red-list?p=1532071#post1532071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As an ST, I suspect they wouldn't look very hard because the people who did it are almost certainly the Banu Haqim's leadership.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can have us or the Setites.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My assumption is that House Carna isn't necessarily Anarch after the Vienna chantry lost its ability to tell the local Prince not to take any aid from its members. Carna being a former Prince herself certainly has the same disdain for Anarchs as most Elders.<br /> <br /> But plenty of Neonates will join the Anarchs among House Carna anyway because it is the best deal if you're not an Elder.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree, and would neither put any of them as Anathema in my own table, just thought they could be possible redders. But, specially the hotel bombing I wouldn't give too much thought, more the Camarilla doing very public actions as to show they aren't going to take an attack like that against their official without response. <br /> <br /> Carna I think would be more suspect during Beckett's Diary since she is dealing with strange stolen magic and leaving a ruckus on her trail. But now, yeah, Camarilla would just want some goddamn Blood Sorcery served at their doorstep, no matter who. Even the blood magic union was broken in this precarious times. Now, wins they who are the lowest bidder (who charges less). <br /> <br /> <br /> And Theo Bell for sure would be listed - don't matter if we believe Hardestadt wanted to be dragon-breathed in front of everyone as part of a big plan or not. Killing a founder is already a great crime, in front of a conclave even worst, the perpetrator being an ex-Archon only accentuates the betrayal. Now... who would be the crazy alastor that chases Bell deep into Anarch ranks, I wouldn't know. After becoming public, Red Listers for me are basically a 'state enemy' list. A statement more than an order of hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T09:31:05-08:00","id":1532088,"title":"","content":"The Followers of Set/Ministry work better with the Anarchs in my personal opinion. There should be some in the Camarilla who are encouraging the other members of the sect to owe them favours, but as a general rule the Anarchs are a better fit as they can guide such passion to there own goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T14:10:17-08:00","id":1532109,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not going to lie, the Camarilla being cheated of the opportunity to host the Setites strikes one as more of boon than a bane!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By the way, thank you everybody for sharing your ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28339,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","user":"Atticus Cleanclaw","date":".  Heartfelt need to show good manners 03-06-2024, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{